        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "subjects. Compared with the subjects born in the non-exposed group, the odds ratio for obesity of the subjects born in 1961 was increased by 38.4% (95% CI: 1.101–1.738) after adjustment of age and sex. The odds ratios of being hyperglycemia are significantly higher in the subjects born in 1960 (1.293 times, 95% CI: 1.041–1.605), 1961 (1.321 times, 95% CI: 1.073–1.626), and 1962 (1.362 times, 95% CI: 1.156–1.604) than the non-exposed group. No positive association was observed in effects of Chinese famine on hypertension among total study population.",
